top -- terms
=============

This directory is William LeFebvre's `top', release 3.3 of 1995-03-02, with a
COHERENT/Z8001 machine module (m_coherent.c) written for this system.  The
portable core -- top.c, display.c, screen.c, commands.c, utils.c, username.c,
version.c and their headers -- is his.

WHERE IT CAME FROM.  ftp://ftp.groupsys.com/pub/top was the author's own
distribution point; the file 01PLACES in every release says so.  That host is
long gone.  The copy taken here is the mirror at

    https://ftp.funet.fi/pub/unix/tools/top/top-3.3.tar.gz
    sha256 478185210e667cad3b44cd50659f40deffb40509dccd127d3cc49849fb8756ed

which is an author-built tarball: its member ownership is `lefebvre/sane'.
3.3 was taken rather than 3.4 (1996) because it is the last release
contemporary with a living COHERENT -- Mark Williams Company folded in 1995 --
and the first to carry the DISCLAIMER file below.

It is NOT a COHERENT holding.  No archive in this project has it, and the
userland inventory's verdict for `top' is none-found; the version above was
fetched from outside the project because nothing inside it has one.

THE GRANT.  Every source file carries this header, and it is the grant:

    Top users/processes display for Unix
    Version 3

    This program may be freely redistributed,
    but this entire comment MUST remain intact.

    Copyright (c) 1984, 1989, William LeFebvre, Rice University
    Copyright (c) 1989, 1990, 1992, William LeFebvre, Northwestern University

top.c additionally opens with

    char *copyright =
        "Copyright (c) 1984 through 1993, William LeFebvre";

which is compiled in and printed by the `h' command, so it travels with the
binary as well as with the source.

EVERY ONE OF THOSE HEADERS IS INTACT in the files here, which is what the
grant asks for.  Nothing was removed from them and nothing was added inside
them; the port's changes are in the code below them.

`freely redistributed' is the whole of the permission.  It says nothing about
modification, and this tree modifies the program: the K&R and 16-bit-int work
the Z8001 needs, the removal of floating point, and the machine module.  Two
things bear on that.  The distribution is built to be modified -- `Porting'
and `m-template' exist for exactly the module written here, and Configure
rewrites top.local.H and Makefile.X in place -- and the author invites the
result back ("please send me a copy", README).  And the same header sits on
every m_*.c in machine/, most of which were contributed by other people, so
the header is what a modified copy is expected to carry, not a bar to making
one.  Recorded as a reading, not as a licence text that says it.

The DISCLAIMER file beside this one is vendored verbatim from the 3.3
distribution and is part of what travels with the code.

THE MACHINE MODULE.  m_coherent.c is new work for this system.  It is not a
port of any m_*.c in the distribution: what it does -- walk procq_ through
/dev/kmem, copy the alloc arena, map chain pointers into this process's own
address space, sum s_size over p_segp[], and read a command line out of the
process's u-area -- was already written and audited here as base/cmd/top.c
before top was adopted, and that file became this one.  It carries the same
BSD-3-Clause position as the rest of the extended system.
